.\" Begin generated content:
.TH "agreety" "1" "2026-03-27"
.PP
.SH "نام (NAME)"
.PP
agreety \- A text-based greeter for greetd
.PP
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.PP
\fBagreety\fR [options]
.PP
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.PP
\fB-h, --help\fR
.RS 4
Show help message and quit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-c, --cmd <command>\fR
.RS 4
Specifies the command to run on successful login.\& agreety will ask if none is
specified.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-f, --max-failures <num>\fR
.RS 4
Specifies the maximum number of login failures to accept before terminating.\&
Defaults to 5.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.PP
agreety is a very simple text-based greeter, with an appearance similar to
\fBagetty\fR(8) and \fBlogin\fR(1).\& It is bundled with \fBgreetd\fR(1).\&
.PP
To use agreety, configure it as your greeter in your greetd config file.\&
.PP
.SH "نویسندگان (AUTHORS)"
.PP
Maintained by Kenny Levinsen <contact@kl.\&wtf>.\& For more information about
greetd development, see https://git.\&sr.\&ht/\(tikennylevinsen/greetd.\&
.PP
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
\fBgreetd\fR(1) \fBgreetd\fR(5)